From: Nathan Rajlich <n@n8.io>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2026 02:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: add HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV, use for RTL8761B

RTL8761B/BU firmware advertises LE Extended Advertising support but
implements it unreliably. Observed in the field on RTL8761BU (TP-Link
UB500, 2357:0604) across months of appliance use:

 - HCI_OP_LE_SET_EXT_ADV_PARAMS (0x2036) intermittently fails -EBUSY
   while connections are active, mirroring the extended-scan failures
   fixed by 5ead2063611a ("Bluetooth: btrtl: fix RTL8761B/BU broken
   LE extended scan");
 - spec-violating LE_EXT_ADV_SET_TERM events with error status
   ("Unexpected advertising set terminated event" spam);
 - advertising sets that silently stop being broadcast while the host
   still believes them active, after connect/disconnect activity.

Add HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV, mirroring HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_SCAN,
gate ext_adv_capable() on it so the host falls back to legacy
advertising (which this firmware handles correctly, with BlueZ
software-multiplexing instances), and set it for CHIP_ID_8761B.

[boompi: experimental local patch; upstream submission candidate as
the sibling of 5ead2063611a if field results hold.]
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
index 4e702b4..fa12f64 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
@@ -1305,9 +1305,12 @@ void btrtl_set_quirks(struct hci_dev *hdev, struct btrtl_device_info *btrtl_dev)
 		/* RTL8761B/BU reports HCI version 5.1 but does not support
 		 * the LE Extended Scan commands (Opcode 0x2042), causing
 		 * repeated -EBUSY failures when BlueZ attempts extended
-		 * scanning while a connection is active.
+		 * scanning while a connection is active. Its extended
+		 * advertising is equally unreliable (spurious set-terminated
+		 * events, sets silently dropped from the air).
 		 */
 		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_SCAN, &hdev->quirks);
+		set_bit(HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV, &hdev->quirks);
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
diff --git a/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h b/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
index 77a3040..ba12b63 100644
--- a/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
+++ b/include/net/bluetooth/hci.h
@@ -272,6 +272,17 @@ enum {
 	 */
 	HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_SCAN,
 
+	/*
+	 * When this quirk is set, the LE Extended Advertising commands are
+	 * not used and the host falls back to legacy advertising. This is
+	 * required for controllers (e.g. RTL8761B) which claim extended
+	 * advertising support but implement it unreliably.
+	 *
+	 * This quirk can be set before hci_register_dev is called or
+	 * during the hdev->setup vendor callback.
+	 */
+	HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV,
+
 	/*
 	 * When this quirk is set, the HCI_OP_GET_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG command is
 	 * disabled. This is required for some Broadcom controllers which
diff --git a/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h b/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
index 4fcee6b..95392f0 100644
--- a/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
+++ b/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
@@ -1878,7 +1878,8 @@ void hci_conn_del_sysfs(struct hci_conn *conn);
 #define use_ext_conn(dev) (((dev)->commands[37] & 0x80) && \
 	!test_bit(HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_CREATE_CONN, &(dev)->quirks))
 /* Extended advertising support */
-#define ext_adv_capable(dev) (((dev)->le_features[1] & HCI_LE_EXT_ADV))
+#define ext_adv_capable(dev) (((dev)->le_features[1] & HCI_LE_EXT_ADV) && \
+			      !test_bit(HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_EXT_ADV, &(dev)->quirks))
 
 /* Maximum advertising length */
 #define max_adv_len(dev) \
